      "side": 1,
      "message": "There\u0027s a lot going on in this test and it took me a while to figure it out. I\u0027d like to introduce a few named helper functions to assist with understanding this.\n\nMaybe the following structure\n```\nDEF_TEST(...) {\n   // set up AGTM\n   skhdr::Agtm agtm;\n   ...\n   // Maybe hoist this into a static getter?\n   SkColor4f inputTestColors[kNumTestColors] \u003d ...;\n   \n   auto test_shader_matches_nonshader \u003d [r, agtm](\n           float targetedHdrHeadroom,\n           SkColor4f[kNumTestColors] expectedTestColors) {\n       skiatest::ReporterContext ctx(r, SkStringPrintf(\"targetedHdrHeadroom:%f\", targetedHdrHeadroom));\n       auto actualShaderColors \u003d test_shader_impl(targetedHdrHeadroom, agtm, inputTestColors);\n       auto actualNonShaderColors \u003d test_nonshader_impl(targetedHdrHeadroom, agtm, inputTestColors);\n       // assert both equal the expected values\n   };\n   \n   test_shader_matches_nonshader(0.0,\n           {\n           // Maybe some commentary on why these values are accurate\n           // or how they were verified. \n            {0.565302f, 0.565302f, 0.565302f, 1.f},\n            {0.565302f, 0.282651f, 0.141326f, 1.f},\n            // Note that we max out at 1.0 because 0.0 means ...\n            {1.000000f, 1.000000f, 1.000000f, 1.f},\n            {0.250000f, 0.500000f, 1.000000f, 1.f},\n            {0.282651f, 0.282651f, 0.282651f, 1.f},\n            {0.815278f, 0.815278f, 0.815278f, 1.f},\n        }\n   );\n   \n   ...\n\n}\n```\nI think those few extra helper functions will make a big scary test seem a lot more inspectable.",
